---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Observatory Computing & Networking — Jack Riconosciuto">
  <div class="container prose">
    <div class="eyebrow">Infrastructure · FreeBSD · Networking · Storage</div>
    <h1>Observatory Computing & Networking</h1>
    <p class="lede">A local computing and storage system for an astrophotography club, built around repurposed hardware and designed for large RAW image datasets.</p>

    <div class="meta">
      <div><span class="meta-label">Platform</span>FreeBSD</div>
      <div><span class="meta-label">Network</span>Wired LAN + Wi‑Fi</div>
      <div><span class="meta-label">Focus</span>Storage / Services</div>
    </div>

    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>I designed and implemented the observatory's computing and networking infrastructure independently, with one exception: I worked with a friend on the physical construction of the server computer itself. The resulting system gives students a shared local environment for storing and processing large astrophotography files.</p>

    <p>The server is a repurposed “Frankenstein” PC assembled from discarded school computers. It runs FreeBSD and provides shared storage and a simple web-based file interface over the observatory's local network.</p>

    <h2>System architecture</h2>
    <div class="architecture" aria-label="Observatory local network architecture">
      <div class="campus-node">CAMPUS NETWORK</div>
      <div class="connector">│</div>
      <div class="router-node">ROUTER</div>
      <div class="connector">│</div>
      <div class="lan-label">OBSERVATORY LAN</div>
      <div class="lan-box">
        <div class="wired-column">
          <div class="branch-label">WIRED ETHERNET</div>
          <div class="device-row">
            <div class="device">
              <strong>FreeBSD Server</strong>
              <span>RAW storage · HTTP file service</span>
            </div>
            <div class="device">
              <strong>3 × iMacs</strong>
              <span>Windows / macOS · processing software</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wifi-column">
          <div class="branch-label">WI‑FI</div>
          <div class="device">
            <strong>Student laptops</strong>
            <span>Local access to shared files and services</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Storage and file service</h2>
    <p>Astrophotography produces very large RAW files, so the server is both a shared repository and a useful place to centralize processing data. Students can access files from the wired iMacs or from laptops connected to the local network over Wi‑Fi.</p>

    <div class="pipeline" aria-label="File storage pipeline">
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>01</span><strong>Upload</strong><small>Client sends file over HTTP</small></div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>02</span><strong>Compress</strong><small>Server losslessly compresses data</small></div>
      <div class="pipeline-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="pipeline-step"><span>03</span><strong>Store</strong><small>Compressed data remains on server</small></div>
    </div>

    <p class="secondary-pipeline"><strong>Download:</strong> stored data is decompressed by the server before being returned to the client.</p>

    <h2>What I built</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Configured and maintained the FreeBSD server and its local services.</li>
      <li>Designed the observatory's local network around a wired LAN with Wi‑Fi access for student laptops.</li>
      <li>Connected the server and three repurposed iMacs to the wired LAN.</li>
      <li>Created a simple local web interface that provides a Google Drive-style file experience over HTTP.</li>
      <li>Designed the storage workflow around large RAW astrophotography files.</li>
      <li>Implemented lossless compression on uploads and automatic decompression on downloads, using spare server CPU capacity to reduce storage requirements.</li>
      <li>Configured the three iMacs for Windows/macOS dual boot and preloaded them with astrophotography processing software.</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Project ownership</strong>
      <p>I designed and implemented the computing, networking, storage, and software infrastructure independently. The physical construction of the server was collaborative.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="photo-placeholder">
      <span class="placeholder-label">PHOTO — TO BE ADDED</span>
      <p>A photo of the server, network setup, or observatory workstation can go here.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">This project has no public GitHub repository. This case study is therefore the primary technical record of the system.</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .architecture {
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid #d8d8d8;
    background: #fafaf8;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
  }

  .campus-node,
  .router-node,
  .device {
    border: 1px solid #222;
    background: white;
  }

  .campus-node,
  .router-node {
    display: inline-flex;
    min-height: 2.8rem;
    padding: .65rem 1.1rem;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    font-size: .76rem;
  }

  .router-node {
    border-color: var(--accent, #176b68);
    color: var(--accent, #176b68);
  }

  .connector {
    height: 1.7rem;
    line-height: 1.7rem;
    color: #777;
  }

  .lan-label {
    display: inline-block;
    margin: .5rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--accent, #176b68);
    font-size: .72rem;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
  }

  .lan-box {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid #bbb;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .wired-column,
  .wifi-column {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .wired-column {
    padding-right: 1rem;
    border-right: 1px solid #ddd;
  }

  .branch-label {
    margin-bottom: .65rem;
    font-size: .66rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    color: #666;
  }

  .device-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: .75rem;
  }

  .device {
    display: grid;
    gap: .35rem;
    padding: .85rem;
  }

  .device strong {
    font-size: .78rem;
    letter-spacing: .02em;
  }

  .device span {
    color: #666;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: .67rem;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .pipeline {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr;
    gap: .8rem;
    align-items: stretch;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .pipeline-step {
    display: grid;
    gap: .35rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid #d8d8d8;
    background: #fafaf8;
  }

  .pipeline-step span {
    color: var(--accent, #176b68);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: .7rem;
  }

  .pipeline-step strong {
    font-size: .9rem;
  }

  .pipeline-step small {
    color: #666;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .pipeline-arrow {
    align-self: center;
    color: #888;
  }

  .secondary-pipeline {
    padding-left: 1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent, #176b68);
  }

  .photo-placeholder {
    min-height: 12rem;
    margin: 3rem 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 2rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    align-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    border: 1px dashed #aaa;
    background: #fafaf8;
  }

  .placeholder-label {
    color: var(--accent, #176b68);
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: .7rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
  }

  .photo-placeholder p {
    margin: .7rem 0 0;
    color: #666;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .architecture {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .lan-box,
    .device-row,
    .pipeline {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .wired-column {
      padding-right: 0;
      padding-bottom: 1rem;
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
    }

    .pipeline-arrow {
      transform: rotate(90deg);
    }
  }
</style>
